#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14079b03-66c0-5657-8909-a7d5ea35bfc0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of Parabola Given Its Parametric Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0ce42e4-a7d5-57da-b3dd-eb27f70938d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0ce42e4-a7d5-57da-b3dd-eb27f70938d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357192} :answer-field/id #uuid "767456eb-e8d8-5700-beb7-2079e41ff6b7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40743546-cb8e-5497-97a4-a66504271cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40743546-cb8e-5497-97a4-a66504271cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357194} :answer-field/id #uuid "73ea54b2-2395-5bdf-9780-650ffe63c4ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f54dfea7-1ce0-53bf-b599-41fdc4b47216" :question/math-academy-id "q-323209" :question/problem "Consider the following parametric equation of the parabola\n\n$$\nx+7=-3t,\\,y-2=-9{t}^{2},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this parabola is\n\n$(x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =-\\frac{x+7}{3},\\,{t}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{9}(y-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{x+7}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{9}(y-2)$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{9} & =-\\frac{1}{9}(y-2) \\\\ {(x+7)}^{2} & =-(y-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
